 kidney disease according to the kidney  foundation the need for organs every  year greater than the number of donors  last year more than four thousand  canadians were waiting for a transplant  heart lung liver or kidney 280 patients  died waiting for their transplant and of  the four thousand still waiting 78  percent needed kidneys but a medical  breakthrough can also raise ethical  questions some may object for religious  reasons others uncomfortable harvesting  organs from pigs even though millions of  pigs are already raised to feed humans  one of the considerations really is that  these  uh highly evolved animals they have the  capacity to feel pain and to suffer it's  not resolved by saying well we're eating  pigs every day because that begs the  question whether we should be eating  them every day doctors say the next step  would be transplant surgeries to extend  the lives of the living to improve  quality of life for a year or longer and  reduce the number who are waiting and  dying without a transplant at all eric  sorenson global news toronto  facebook's new chapter next the  company's ambitious plan to rebrand  facebook has faced a ton of criticism  for allowing hate and misinformation to  spread on the platform and profiting  from it and now its ceo is reported to  be on the verge of rebranding his  company mark zuckerberg has said the key  to facebook's future is something called  the metaverse if you don't know what  that is you are not alone here's jackson  proskow  facebook revolutionized the way we  connect the company's next big step  could be one that changes everything  about online they see the writing on the  wall they see that they need to evolve  themselves tech website the verge  reports facebook is getting ready to  rebrand with a new name and new focus  the company declined to comment to  global news the facebook site along with  instagram and whatsapp would be  platforms operated by a parent company  that's built around something bigge